+
+#### `importPackageWithLog`
+
+*   Like `importPackage` but returns a rich import-log summary instead of a boolean.
+    Useful for verifying the import actually changed the collection (counts of
+    new / updated / duplicate / conflicting notes, plus the post-import deck count).
+
+    Requires Anki 23.10+ (uses `col.import_anki_package`). Raises on older Anki
+    versions; use `importPackage` instead.
+
+    Parameters:
+    - `path` *(required)*: path to the .apkg file, as seen from Anki's process.
+    - `mergeNotetypes` *(default `false`)*: if true, merge matching notetypes
+      from the import into existing ones rather than creating duplicates.
+    - `updateNotes` *(default `"IF_NEWER"`)*: one of `"IF_NEWER"`, `"ALWAYS"`,
+      `"NEVER"`. Controls whether existing notes are updated from the import.
+    - `updateNotetypes` *(default `"IF_NEWER"`)*: same options as `updateNotes`,
+      applied to notetypes rather than notes.
+    - `withScheduling` *(default `true`)*: import scheduling state (review
+      history, intervals) from the package.
+    - `withDeckConfigs` *(default `true`)*: import deck configurations from
+      the package.
+
+    <details>
+    <summary><i>Sample request:</i></summary>
+
+    ```json
+    {
+        "action": "importPackageWithLog",
+        "version": 6,
+        "params": {
+            "path": "/data/Deck.apkg",
+            "updateNotes": "IF_NEWER"
+        }
+    }
+    ```
+    </details>
+
+    <details>
+    <summary><i>Sample result:</i></summary>
+
+    ```json
+    {
+        "result": {
+            "found_notes": 42,
+            "new": 40,
+            "updated": 2,
+            "duplicate": 0,
+            "conflicting": 0,
+            "deck_count_after": 5
+        },
+        "error": null
+    }
+    ```
     </details>
 
